

1. Add an Account in Chart of Accounts
Step 1:
Go to Chart of Accounts UI or use API to add a new account:

Code: 1130
Name: Petty Cash
Type: ASSET
Parent: 1110 (Cash)
Expected:

Account appears in the list.
Can be selected as a default account for payments.
2. Payment Creation and Allocation
Step 2:
Create a customer payment:

Party: Acme Corporation (60b23cd6-744b-495f-98e7-4730a6c1c1f9)
Payment Type: Customer_Payment
Amount: 4450.00
Payment Mode: bank
Status: Draft
Step 3:
Allocate payment to invoice:

Invoice: INV-SEED-001 (d0000001-0001-4000-a000-000000000005)
Allocated Amount: 4450.00
Expected:

Allocation is saved.
Cannot confirm payment if allocation is missing.
3. Confirm Payment and Journal Entry
Step 4:
Confirm the payment.

Expected:

Status changes to Confirmed.
Journal entry is created:
Debit: Bank Account (from default accounts, e.g., 1110)
Credit: Accounts Receivable (1120)
Journal entry lines reference correct accounts and amounts.
4. Cancel Payment
Step 5:
Cancel the confirmed payment.

Expected:

Status changes to Cancelled.
Reversal journal entry is created (debits/credits swapped).
5. Supplier Payment Flow
Step 6:
Create a supplier payment:

Party: TechWorld Supplies (a1b2c3d4-1111-4aaa-bbbb-000000000001)
Payment Type: Supplier_Payment
Amount: 13150.00
Payment Mode: bank
Status: Draft
Step 7:
Allocate payment to supplier invoice:

Invoice: INV-SEED-002 (e0000001-0001-4000-a000-000000000005)
Allocated Amount: 13150.00
Step 8:
Confirm the payment.

Expected:

Status changes to Confirmed.
Journal entry is created:
Debit: Accounts Payable (2010)
Credit: Bank Account (1110)
6. Edge Cases
Try confirming payment with missing default accounts (should fail).
Try allocating more than payment amount (should fail).
Try cancelling a payment that is not confirmed (should fail).
7. Seed Data for Invoices
Use /core-service/scripts/seed_full_flow.sql to ensure you have:
5 customer invoices (e.g., INV-SEED-001)
5 supplier invoices (e.g., INV-SEED-002)
Use the UUIDs and party IDs from the script for realistic test data.



