2. Set Default Accounts
Default Account Types to Set:

cash (e.g., 1100)
accounts_receivable (e.g., 1200)
accounts_payable (e.g., 2100)
sales (e.g., 3100)
office_supplies (e.g., 4100)
Manual Steps:

Go to the Default Accounts or System Configuration section.
For each transaction type, select the appropriate account from the list.
Example: Set "cash" default to "Cash and Bank" (1100).
Example: Set "accounts_receivable" default to "Accounts Receivable" (1200).
Save and verify that the mapping is correct.